        <p>MESSRS. CROSFIED'S MAIN.—A bowling main, in con- nection with Messrs. Crostield and Sous Athletic Club, was held on Saturday on the Stag Inn green. The main was confined to Messrs. Crosfteld'i; employes, and there was a record entry—one hundred and twenty-two taking part in the proceedings. The following were the prize winners: 1, Alfred Davies ; 2, T. Wright ;3. W. E. Clegg; 4, E. Gleave; 5, C. Sutcliffe; 6, J. Howard ; 7, J. Middleton; 8, W. Gibbons ~ 9, D. Smith ; 10, W. Stokes; 11, T. Taylor ;..12, G.Aston ; 13, T. Davies : 14, D. Stokes; 15, J. Hill ; 16, J. Hollingsworth. Sub- stantial prizes had been offered and these were dis- tributediu Mossrs.Crosfield's assembly room on Tuesday by Dr. Markel. LIBERAL CLUB V. CONSERVATIVE CLUIL—The return match between the Liberal and Conservative Clubs was played on the Liberal Club green on Saturday. Scores : LIBERALS. CONSERVATIVES. S. D. S. D. T. Critchley ll 1 J. Taylor H. Daintith M. Tobin F. Baker T. Bandies D. Whitfield ll .1 T. Cooper G i W Daintith Orrrd re 11 }l3 F. Rutter iJ. Davies !IL Kerr lOl /3 J. Hesketh iE. J. Mitchell jE. J. Mitchell lll J. Ashton 2 1 Is IJ. Houghton I W Daintith lien'dk st iii 13 W. Hill j. Parr F. A. Sanders ll 113 W. J. Wilson A. Lawten W. Patrick . Twiss C. Jordan F. Morrell W. Taylor ll J M. Allen ...... ...... 8 )</p>
