      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-08-26_WidnesExaminer_art0138" n="art0138">
        <head>FLOWER SHOWS.</head>
        <p>FLOWER SHOWS.</p>
        <p>Stockton Heath.</p>
        <p>Since its inception the Stockton Heath Garden Society has made rapid strides and the annual show in connection with the Society, which was held on Satur- day, was in every way a success. In past years the exhibits have been accommodated in the Church Institute but so great was the demand upon space this year that a large marquee had to ba utilised in addition to that building. The exhibits, which showed a large increase upon previous years, had been artistically arranged and the pleasing effect produced was greatly added to by a display of hot-house plants lent for the occasion by Sir Gilbert and Lady Greenall, Mrs. Lyon, Mr. Vere B. Davies, r. W. Long, Mr. G. Starkey, and Mr. G. Tardy, and choice orchids sent by the Mayor of Warrington. The quality of the exhibits was good especially in the vegetable classes. Competition in the classes for cottage gardens &amp;c.was unusually keen and throughout comp3titors have made the best possible use of the material at their disposal. An attractive feature of the show was an excellent programme of musia which was, during the afternoon, submitted by local artistes. Those contributing :—Mrs. C. J. Holmes, Mrs. A. J. ‘Villett, Miss Birtles, Miss Bouchier, Miss Marie Houghton, Miss Florence E. Brown, Miss Maggie Gandy, and Messrs. Walter Howard and A. Hale. The judging of the exhibits gave general satisfaction and in thts respect the following are to be thanked for the able manner in which they discharged their duties:— Mrs. Lyon, Mrs. Pigot, and Mrs. W. B. Roberts; Mr. Moore, Mr. F. Timperley and Mr. Ryan; and Mr. Lockhart and Mr. Slater.</p>
        <p>I The opening ceremony was performed by Mrs Lyon ;in the presence of a large assembly, the Rev. H. V. Pigot presiding. Mrs. Lyon congratulated the Society upon its success which she hoped would be continued. Opportunity was taken of according votes of thanks to Mrs. Lyon, the judges, the entertainers, Mr. Fawcett (hon. secretary), and Mr. Pigot for his services in the , chair.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-08-26_WidnesExaminer_art0139" n="art0139">
        <head>PRIZE LIST.</head>
